Reason:
The code attempts to find a class associated with the given port ID but only checks the immediate child classes of the Qdisc. This oversight means that if filters are installed on the parent Qdisc instead of the immediate child classes, those filters will be missed, leading to incomplete reverse binding in complex class hierarchies.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
args.w.fn = tc_bind_class_walker;
q->ops->cl_ops->walk(q, &args.w);
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a new function `tc_bind_class_walker` that traverses all child classes of the Qdisc, ensuring that all relevant filters are considered for reverse binding. This change allows the code to correctly handle complex class hierarchies by walking through all child classes, thus preventing the omission of necessary filters.

